From 57cd900b909162edc8749abee435190fa5a7c393 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aryan Kadole <aryan.kadole@espressif.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 18:21:12 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Add usrsctp_snap_establish(): open the association from
 the peer's INIT

The peer's INIT is applied as an INIT-ACK would be and the association
opened as by a COOKIE-ACK, with the lower layer's round trip as the
first RTT measurement (draft-uberti-tsvwg-warp, section 4.1). Until
then, what the peer sends is dropped, except an INIT or ABORT, and an
INIT that can not be applied aborts the association.
